TEXT -416 160 Left 2 !.tran 0 100s 0 0.6ms
TEXT -416 168 Left 2 !.param tdv=1 tdt=1 fn1=50 omega_n={2*pi*fn1}\n.options vntol=10 abstol=100m reltol=0.003
TEXT 272 184 Left 2 ;General:\n \nThis model is a synchronous generator:\nThe speed is regulated externally by speed controller\nThe voltage is regulated externally by AVR (automatic voltage regulator)\n \n \n \nparams:\n            UN_verkettet=20000 Nominal voltage\n            IN=14.434k Nominal current\n            Pel=400e6 Nominal power (cos phi=0.8)\n            Kc=0.5 short-circuit ratio (0.5 cylindrical pole, 0.8-1.0 salient pole)\n            UE0=600V Nominal field voltage\n            IE0=2000A Nominal field current\n             p=2 Number of polepairs    \n             Schenkelpolfactor=1                                        \n             Daempferfaktor=1 (damping factor)\n             Streuung=0.05 (leakage factor)\n             rcu=0.01 (rel. Copper resistance)\n             rbg=0.001 (rel. friction moment)\n             J=100000 (inertia)\n             a=0.9 (for nonlinear magnetizing curve)\n             m=7  (for nonlinear magnetizing curve)\n \nAlternative Elements: none\n          \nHINT: The power output can be computed with M*314.159/2  (P=M*omega/p)\n                    The load angle can be outputed with V(u6:theta)\n                    The constant frequency is n/30    2*n/60 = p*n/60 (p=Polcount)\n \nLibfile: Sgen.lib
TEXT -416 0 Left 4 ;Measurement of Generator Rotational energy:\nThe generator feeds the load with 100MW \nAt 10s the speed controller is off and the Turbine\npower is zero. The machine slows now down till \nspeed is zero. The rotational energy is consumed \nnow by the powerlost due to the load.\nHINT: Set the horizontal axis starting from 10s to 100s \nFor measurement of the rotational energy ALT/(ALT Gr)+Click on the load element\nThen Ctrl+Click on the generated trace
TEXT -184 328 Left 2 ;For voltage regulation there is a AVR\nIt is enabled from 3.5s because then the\ngenerator output voltage reach their nominal\nvalue. You can see that the voltage drops at\nswitching the load and later is compensated\nby increasing the field voltage of the machine
TEXT -264 472 Left 2 ;Speed regulator is on at from the beginning\nAt 4s there is a load step of 100MW\nsee load angle V(u6:theta) of approx. 8 degrees
TEXT -384 264 Left 2 ;Internal load angle = V(u6:theta)
TEXT 80 384 Left 2 ;After 4s there is a load step \nof 100MW
TEXT 80 368 Left 2 !.param PN=100e6 QN=0
TEXT -320 536 Left 2 ;Torque
TEXT -240 536 Left 2 ;Friction torque
TEXT -96 288 Left 2 ;3.5s
TEXT -112 272 Left 2 ;4.0s
TEXT -128 256 Left 2 ;20000v
TEXT -416 464 Left 2 ;1500
TEXT -288 496 Left 2 ;1
TEXT -112 432 Left 2 !Vm m1 0 pwl 0s 0
TEXT -24 456 Left 2 ;Computation of the rotating energy of the generator by hand:\nLength of rotor = 10m\nRadius of rotor = 0.7m\nVolume in cubic meter = 15.393 (radius*radius*pi*length)\nMass in kg: Volume*specific mass index (about 8) \nM=8.0*Volume*10*10*10=123150kg = 123 tons\nJrotor=Inertia=M*radius*radius=60343 (rotor)\nJturbine=40000 (Inertia of the turbine)\nJ=Jrotor+Jturbine=100000 (see generator input)\nPolepair p=2 (4 poles)\nomega_mech=omega_el/p=314.159/2=157.08 (50Hz)\nErot=0.5*J*omega_mech^2 (Rotational energy)\nErot=1.233 GJ (see also with Ctrl+Click on Powerline of load - but at first set the horizontal axis from 10s to 100s)\nFor the computation see the wxMaxima file \nRotationalEnergy.wxmx (Lost of stator resistance not considered in this example)
TEXT -416 376 Left 2 ;After 10s the speed controller is off\nNow the generator has no turbine\nouther torque is zero
TEXT -176 152 Left 2 ;Hint: You can derive even better accuracy by\nchanging max. timestep to 0.1ms vntol to 100m abstol to 1m reltol to 0.001
TEXT 256 136 Left 2 ;See also rotatinal_energy.asc in this folder\nsomehow like this example
TEXT -104 400 Left 2 ;10s
TEXT -264 408 Left 2 ;10s
